description:
Come along and enjoy our fun school holiday activities!
Matariki Lantern Magic |&nbsp;Wednesday 8 July, 10am - 11am&nbsp;
Enjoy papercraft with the stars!
Worm Farming For Kids Workshop |&nbsp;Thursday 16 July, 10.30am - 11.30am
Join Laura (from Compost Collective) for a fun hands-on worm farming workshop for kids and whānau. Children will meet tiger worms and learn how they turn food scraps into fertiliser.
These events are recommended for children aged 3-12 and they must be accompanied by an adult.&nbsp;

Create your own map of the Matariki stars that you can hang up in your window letting you enjoy the stars even in the daytime.
Children must be supervised by a parent or guardian at all times.&nbsp;
No booking required - just drop in to the Auckland Botanic Gardens Visitor Centre.
